  "title": "Mary Seacole",
  "summary": "Born Mary Jane Grant in Jamaica in 1805, Seacole paid for her own trip to the Crimea in 1855 and, with Thomas Day, set up the British Hotel near Balaclava, which served as storehouse, canteen and resting place for the army. She was declared bankrupt after returning to England. Her autobiography appeared in July 1857, and she died in London in 1881.",
